#import "../../../proofs.typ": speech, footnote

== 1. Introduction

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 1]: What is thy only comfort in Life and Death?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That both in Soul and#footnote[1 Corinthians 6:19; 1 Thessalonians 5:10] Body, whether I live or dye,#footnote[Romans 14:8] I am not mine own, but#footnote[1 Corinthians 3:23] belong wholly unto my most faithful Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ: who by his most precious Blood#footnote[1 Peter 1:18–19; 1 John 1:7; 1 John 2:2] fully satisfying for all my Sins, hath#footnote[1 John 3:8; Hebrews 2:14–15] delivered me from all the power of the Devil, and so#footnote[John 6:39] preserveth me, that without the will of my Heavenly Father not so much as an Hair may#footnote[Matthew 10:30; Luke 21:18] fall from my Head; yea all things#footnote[Romans 8:28] must serve for my safety: wherefore by his Spirit also he#footnote[2 Corinthians 1:12; 2 Corinthians 5:5; Ephesians 1:13–14] assureth me of everlasting Life, and#footnote[Romans 8:24–25] maketh me ready and prepared, that henceforth I may live to him.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 2]: How many things are necessary for thee to know, that thou injoying this comfort mayst live and dye happily?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: #footnote[Luke 24:47; 1 Corinthians 6:11; Romans 8:15; Titus 3:3–8] Three. The first, what is the#footnote[John 4:41; Romans 3] greatness of my sin and misery. The second, how I am#footnote[John 17:3] delivered from all Sin and Misery. The third, what thanks I#footnote[Ephesians 5:10; 1 Peter 2:9; 1 Peter 3:10–12; Romans 6:11–13; Matthew 5:16; Titus 2:11–12] owe unto God for this delivery.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 3]: Whence knowest thou thy misery?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Out of the Law of#footnote[Romans 3:20; Romans 7:5,13; Romans 5:20] God.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 4]: What doth the Law of God require of us?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That which Christ doth summarily teach us, Matthew 22:37–40. Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy Heart, and with all thy Soul, and with all thy Mind, and with all thy#footnote[Luke 10:27] Strength. This is the first and the great Commandment; and the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy Neighbour as thy self. On these two Commandments hang the whole Law and the Prophets.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 5]: Art thou able to keep all these things perfectly?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: No#footnote[Romans 3:10,23; 1 John 1:8] truly: for by nature I am prone to the hatred of God, and of my#footnote[Romans 8:7; Ephesians 2:3; Titus 3:3] Neighbours.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 6]: Did God then make man so wicked and perverse?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Not#footnote[Genesis 1:31] so, but rather he made him good, and to his own#footnote[Genesis 1:26–27] Image; that is, indued with true Righteousness and Holiness, that he might rightly know God his Creator, and heartily love him, and live with him blessed for ever, and that to laud and magnify#footnote[2 Corinthians 3:18; Colossians 3:10; Ephesians 4:24] him.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 7]: Whence then ariseth the wickedness of Mans nature?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: From the fall and disobedience of our first Parents Adam and#footnote[Romans 5:12; Romans 5:18–19] Eve: hence is our nature so corrupt that we are all conceived and born in#footnote[Psalm 51:5; Genesis 5:3] Sin.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 8]: Are we so corrupt that we are not at all apt to do well, and are prone to all vice?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Indeed we are, except we are regenerated by the Holy#footnote[John 3:5; Genesis 6:5; Job 14:4; Job 15:16; Isaiah 53:6] Ghost.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 9]: Doth not God then Injury to Man who in the Law requireth that of him which he is not able to perform?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: No; For God had made Man such a one as#footnote[John 3:5; Ephesians 4:24] he might perform it: but Man by the impulsion of the#footnote[Luke 10:30] Devil, and his own stubbornness bereaved himself and all his posterity of those Divine Graces.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 10]: Doth God leave this stubbornness and falling away of Man unpunished?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: No: but is angry in most dreadful#footnote[Romans 5:12] manner, as well for the sins wherein we are born, as also for those which our selves commit, and in most just Judgment punisheth them with present and everlasting Punishments, as himself pronounceth: Cursed be he that confirmeth not all the words of this Law to do#footnote[Deuteronomy 27:26; Galatians 3:10] them.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 11]: Is not God therefore merciful?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Yea, Verily he is#footnote[Exodus 34:6; Psalm 5:4–6] merciful; but so, that he is also#footnote[Exodus 20:5; 2 Corinthians 6:14] just: wherefore his Justice requireth that the same which is committed against the divine Majesty of God, should also be recompenced with extream, that is, everlasting Punishment both in Body and Soul.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 12]: Seeing then by the just Judgment of God we are subject both to temporal and eternal Punishments, is there yet any way or means remaining whereby we may be delivered from these Punishments, and be reconciled to God?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: God will have his#footnote[Exodus 20:5–7; Exodus 23:7] Justice satisfied: wherefore it is necessary#footnote[Romans 8:3] that we satisfy either by our selves, or by another.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 13]: Are we able to satisfy by our selves?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Not a whit. Nay rather we do every day#footnote[Job 9:2–3; Job 15:15; Matthew 6:12] increase our debt.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 14]: Is there any creature in Heaven or in Earth, which is only a creature, able to satisfy for us?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: None. For first God will#footnote[missing] not punish that Sin in any other creature which man hath committed: and further, neither can that which is nothing but a creature sustain the wrath of God against sin,#footnote[Psalm 130:3; Job 4:18; Job 25:5] and deliver others from it.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 15]: What manner of Mediatour then, and Deliverer must we seek for?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Such a one verily as is very Man, and perfectly just, and yet in Power above all creatures, that is, one who also is very#footnote[1 Corinthians 15:25; Jeremiah 23:6; Isaiah 53:11; 2 Corinthians 5:14; Hebrews 7:16; Isaiah 7:14; Romans 8:3] God.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 16]: Wherefore is it necessary that he be very Man, and that perfectly just too?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Because that the Justice of God requireth that the same humane nature which hath sinned, do it self likewise make recompence for sin: but#footnote[Romans 5:12,17] he that is himself a#footnote[1 Peter 3:18; Hebrews 7:26] sinner, cannot make recompence for others.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 17]: Why must he also be very God?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That he might by the Power of his#footnote[Isaiah 55:3,8; Acts 2:24; 1 Peter 3:18] Godhead sustain in his flesh the burthen of God’s wrath,#footnote[1 John 1:2; 1 John 4:9–10; Acts 20:28; John 3:16] and might recover and restore unto us that Righteousness and Life which we lost.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 18]: And who is that Mediatour which is together both very God, and a very perfectly just Man?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Even our Lord Jesus#footnote[Matthew 1:23; 1 Timothy 3:16; John 14:16; 1 Timothy 2:5; Luke 2:11] Christ, who is made to us of God’s Wisdom, Righteousness, Sanctification#footnote[1 Corinthians 1:30] & Redemption.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 19]: Whence knowest thou this?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Out of the Gospel which God first made known#footnote[Genesis 3:15] in Paradise, and#footnote[Genesis 22:18; Genesis 49:10–11; Romans 1:2; Hebrews 1:1; Acts 3:22; Acts 10:43] afterwards did spread it a broad by the Patriarchs and#footnote[John 5:46; Hebrews 10:7] Prophets: shadowed it by Sacrifices and other Ceremonies of the Law; and#footnote[Romans 10:4; Galatians 4:4; Galatians 3:24; Hebrews 13:8] lastly accomplished it by his only begotten Son Christ our Lord.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 20]: Is then Salvation restored by Christ to all men who perished in Adam?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Not to all: but to those only who by a true Faith are ingrafted into him,#footnote[John 1:12; John 3:36; Isaiah 53:11; Psalm 2:12; Romans 11:20; Hebrews 4:2; Hebrews 10:39] and receive his benefits.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 21]: What is Faith?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: It is not only a knowledg, whereby I surely assent to all things which God#footnote[Hebrews 11:13; James 2:19; Galatians 2:20] hath revealed unto us in his Word, but also an#footnote[Romans 4:16; Romans 5:1; Romans 10:10] hassured trust kindled in#footnote[Romans 1:16; Romans 10:17; 1 Corinthians 1:21; Mark 16:16; Acts 16:14] my heart by the Holy Ghost, through the Gospel, whereby I make my repose in God, being assuredly resolved that Remission of Sins, everlasting#footnote[Matthew 16:17; John 3:5; Galatians 5:22; Philemon 1:19] Righteousness, and life is given not to others only, but to me also, and that freely through the Mercy of God, for#footnote[Romans 3:24–25; Acts 10:45;] for the Merits of Christ alone.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 22]: What are those things which are necessary for a Christian man to believe?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: All things which are promised us in the Gospel: the sum whereof is briefly comprised in the Articles of the Catholick and undoubted Faith of all true Christians, commonly called the Creed. I believe in God the Father Almighty, maker of Heaven and Earth; and in Jesus Christ his only Son, our Lord, which was conceived by the Holy Ghost, born of the Virgin Mary, suffered under Pontius Pilate, was crucified, dead & buried, he descended into Hell; the third day he arose again from the dead, and ascended into Heaven, fro whence he shall come to judge both the quick and the dead. I believe in the Holy Ghost, the Holy Catholick Church, the Communion of Saints, the forgiveness of sins, the Resurrection of the Body, and the life everlasting. Amen.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 23]: Into how many parts is this Creed divided?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Into three: the first of the eternal Father, and our Creation: the second of the Son and our Redemption: the third of the Holy Ghost, and our Sanctification.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 24]: Seing there is but one only substance of God, why namest thou those three, the Father, the Son, and the Holy Ghost?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: #footnote[Deuteronomy 6:4; Ephesians 4:6; Isaiah 44:6; Isaiah 45:5; 1 Corinthians 8:4;] Because God#footnote[Isaiah 61:1; Luke 4:18; Psalm 110:1; Matthew 3:16–17; Matthew 28:19; John 14:26; John 15:26; Titus 3:5–6; Ephesians 2:18; 2 Corinthians 13:14; Galatians 4:6; 1 John 5:7] hath so manifested himself in his Word, that these three distinct Persons are that one true everlasting God.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 25]: What believest thou when thou sayest, I believe in God the Father Almighty, maker of Heaven and Earth?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: I believe the everlasting Father of our Lord Iesus Christ,#footnote[Genesis 1:1–2; Psalm 33:6; Job 33:4; Acts 4:24; Acts 14:15,&c; Isaiah 45:7] who made of nothing Heaven and Earth, with all that are in them; who likewise upholdeth#footnote[Psalm 104:3; Psalm 115:3; Matthew 10:29; Hebrews 1:3; Romans 11:36] and governeth the same by his eternal Counsel and#footnote[John 1:12; Romans 8:15; Galatians 4:5–6; Ephesians 1:5] Providence. This God I believe to be my God and Father for Christ sake; and therefore so trust in him, and rely on him, that I make no doubt but he will provide all#footnote[Psalm 55:23; Matthew 6:26; Luke 12:22] things necessary both for my soul and body; and further, whatsoever evils he sendeth on me in this troublesome life, he#footnote[Romans 8:28] will turn them to my safety; seing both he is able to do it, as being#footnote[Isaiah 46:4; Romans 10:12; Romans 8:38] God Almighty, and willing to do it, as#footnote[missing] being a bountiful Father.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 26]: What is the Providence of God?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: The almighty Power of God, every where#footnote[Acts 17:25; Psalm 94:9; Isaiah 29:15; Ezekiel 8:12] present, whereby he doth as it were by his hand uphold#footnote[Hebrews 1:2–3] and govern Heaven and Earth, with all the Creatures therein, so that those things which grow in the Earth, as likewise rain and drowth, fruitfulness and barenness, meat#footnote[Jeremiah 5:24; Acts 14:17] and#footnote[John 9:3] and drink, health and#footnote[Proverbs 22:2] sickness, riches and poverty; in a word, all things come not rashly and by chance, but by his fatherly Counsel and will.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 27]: What doth this knowledg of the Creation and Providence of God profit us?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That in#footnote[Romans 5:3; Job 1:21] adversity we may be patient,#footnote[Deuteronomy 8:10; 1 Thessalonians 5:18] and thankful in prosperity,#footnote[Romans 5:4–5] and have hereafter our chiefest hope reposed in God our most faithful Father; being sure that there is nothing which#footnote[Romans 8:38; Romans 8:19;] may withdraw us from his love; forasmuch as all creatures are so in his Power, that without his Will they are#footnote[Job 1:12; Job 2:6; Proverbs 21:1; Acts 17:27,&c] not able not only to do any thing, but not so much as once to move.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 28]: Why is the Son of God called Jesus, that is, a Saviour?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Because he saveth us from our#footnote[Matthew 1:21] sins; neither ought any safety to be sought for from any other,#footnote[Hebrews 7:25; Acts 4:12] nor can elsewhere be found.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 29]: Do they then believe in the only Saviour Jesus, who seek for happiness and safety of the Saints, or of themselves, or else where?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: No: for although in word they boast themselves of him as their only Saviour, yet indeed they deny the only#footnote[1 Corinthians 1:13,30,&c] Saviour Jesus: for it must needs be that either Jesus is not a perfect Saviour, or that those who imbrace him as their Saviour with a true faith, possess all things in him#footnote[Hebrews 12:2; Isaiah 9:6; Colossians 1:19–20; Colossians 2:10; Isaiah 43:11,25; John 1:16] which are required unto Salvation.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 30]: Why is he called Christ, that is, anointed?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Because he was ordained of the Father, and anointed of the holy Ghost#footnote[Psalm 45:7; Hebrews 1:9; Deuteronomy 18:15; Acts 3:22] the chief Prophet#footnote[John 1:18; John 15:15; Matthew 11:27] and Teacher, who#footnote[Hebrews 7:21; Hebrews 10:12] hath opened unto us the secret Counsel, & all the will of his Father concerning our Redemption, and the high Preist, who with that one only Sacrifice of his Body#footnote[Romans 3:24; Romans 5:9–10] hath redeemed us, and doth#footnote[Psalm 2:6; Luke 1:33] continually make Intercession to his Father for us; and a King, who ruleth us by his Word and Spirit, and defendeth#footnote[Matthew 28:18] and maintaineth that Salvation which he hath purchased for us.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 31]: But why art thou called a Christian?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Because through Faith I am a member of#footnote[Acts 11:26; 1 Corinthians 6:15] Jesus Christ,#footnote[1 John 2:27; Isaiah 59:2; 1 John 2:28] and partaker of his anointing, that both I#footnote[Matthew 10:33] may confess his name, and present my self unto him#footnote[Romans 12:1; Revelation 5:8; 1 Peter 2:5; 2 Timothy 2:12; Romans 6:12–13; Revelation 1:6] a lively Sacrifice of thankfulness, and also may in this life fight against Sin and Satan with free and good conscience, and#footnote[1 Timothy 1:18–19] afterwards enjoy an everlasting Kingdom with Christ.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 32]: For what cause is Christ called the only begotten Son of God, when we also are the Sons of God?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Because Christ alone is the eternal and natural Son of the#footnote[Hebrews 1:2–3; John 3:16] eternal Father, and#footnote[Romans 8:3; Ephesians 1:6; John 1:12; 1 John 1:3] we are but Sons adopted of the Father by Grace for his sake.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 33]: Wherefore callest thou him our Lord?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Because he redeeming and ransoming both our Body and Soul from Sin, not with Gold nor Silver, but with his precious Blood, and delivering us from all the Power of the Devil, hath set#footnote[1 Peter 1:18; 1 Corinthians 6:20; Ephesians 1:7; 1 Timothy 2:5–6; Romans 14:9] us free to serve him.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 34]: What believest thou when thou sayest, He was conceived by the Holy Ghost, and born of the Virgin Mary?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That the Son of God, who#footnote[missing] is and continueth true and#footnote[Romans 9:5; Isaiah 7:14; Isaiah 9:6; 1 John 5:20; John 20:28] everlasting#footnote[John 1:14; Galatians 4:4] God, took the#footnote[Romans 1:3] very Nature of man, of the flesh and blood of the Virgin Mary, through the working of the#footnote[missing] Holy-Ghost, that withal he might be the true Seed of#footnote[Philippians 2:7; Hebrews 4:15; Hebrews 7:26] David, like unto his Brethren in all things#footnote[missing] Sin excepted.#footnote[missing]]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 35]: What profit takest thou by Christ’s holy Conception and Nativity?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That he is our#footnote[Hebrews 2:16–17] Mediator, and doth cover with his Innocency and perfect Holiness my Sins, in which I was conceived, that they may not come in the Sight of#footnote[Psalm 32:1; 1 Corinthians 1:30; Romans 8:3–4; Galatians 4:4–5] God.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 36]: What believest thou when thou sayest he suffered.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That he all the time of his life which he lead in the Earth, but especially at the end#footnote[1 Peter 2:4; 1 Peter 3:18; Isaiah 53:12] thereof, sustained the wrath of God, both in body and soul, against the sin of mankind, that he might by his passion, as the#footnote[1 John 2:2; 1 John 4:10] only propitiatory sacrifice, deliver our body and soul from everlasting damnation, and purchase us the favour of God, righteousness, and everlasting life.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 37]: For what cause should he suffer under Pilate, as being his Judg?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That he being innocent#footnote[Luke 23:14; John 19:4] and condemned before a civil Judg#footnote[Psalm 69:4; Isaiah 53:4–5; 2 Corinthians 5:21; Galatians 3:13] might deliver us from the severe Judgment of God which remained for all men.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 38]: But is there any more in it, that he was fastened to the Cross, than if he had suffered any other kind of death?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: There is more: for by this I am assured that he took upon himself the curse which did ly on me; for the death of the Cross#footnote[Deuteronomy 21:23; Galatians 3:13] was accursed of God.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 39]: Why was it necessary for Christ to humble himself unto death?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Because the Justice and Truth of God could by#footnote[Genesis 2:17] no other means be satisfied for our sins, but by the very death of the#footnote[Hebrews 2:9,14–15; Philippians 2:8] Son of God.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 40]: To what end was he buried also?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That thereby he might manifest that he#footnote[Acts 13:29; Matthew 27:60; Luke 23:53; John 19:38] was dead indeed.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 41]: But since that Christ died for us, why must we also die?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Our death is not a satisfaction for our Sins, but the abolishing of Sin, and our passage#footnote[John 5:24; 1 Philippians 23; Romans 7:24] into everlasting Life.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 42]: What other commodity receive we by the Death of Christ?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That by the virtue of his Death our old man is crucified, slain, and#footnote[Romans 6:6] buried together with him, (figured out in holy Baptism) that henceforth evil lusts and desires may#footnote[Romans 6:12] not reign in us, but we#footnote[Romans 12:1] may offer our selves unto him a Sacrifice of thanksgiving.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 43]: Why is there added, he descended into Hell?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That in my greatest pains and most grevious temptations I may support my self with this comfort, that my Lord Jesus Christ#footnote[Isaiah 53:10; Matthew 27:46] hath delivered me (by the unspeakable distresses, torments and terrors of his Soul, into which he was plunged both before, and then especially when he hanged on the Cross) from the straits and torments of Hell.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 44]: What doth the Resurrection of Christ profit us?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: First, by his Resurrection he vanquished death, that he#footnote[1 Corinthians 15:6; 1 Corinthians 5:4–6; Romans 4:25; 1 Peter 1:3,&c and 21] might make us partakers of that Righteousness which he had gotten us by his death. Again, we are now#footnote[Romans 6:4; Colossians 3:1,&c; Ephesians 2:5] also stirred up by his Power to a new Life. Lastly, the Resurrection of our head, Christ, is a#footnote[1 Corinthians 15:12,&c; Romans 8:11] Pledg unto us of our glorious Resurrection.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 45]: How understand you that he ascended into Heaven?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That Christ, his Disciples looking on, was#footnote[Acts 1:9; Mark 16:19; Luke 24:51] taken up from the Earth into Heaven, and yet#footnote[Hebrews 4:14; Hebrews 7:25; Hebrews 9:11; Romans 8:34; Ephesians 4:10; Colossians 3:1] still is there for our sakes, and will be until he come again to judge the quick and#footnote[Acts 1:11; Matthew 24:30] the dead.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 46]: Is not Christ with us then until the end of the World, as he hath promised?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: #footnote[Matthew 28:20; Matthew 26:11; John 16:18; John 17:11; Acts 3:21] Christ is true God, and true Man, and so according to his Manhood is not now on Earth, but according to his Godhead, his Majesty, his Grace, and#footnote[John 14:17,&c; John 16:13; Ephesians 4:8] Spirit is at no time from us.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 47]: Are not by this means the two natures in Christ pulled assunder, if his Humanity be not wheresoever his Divinity is?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: No; for seeing his Divinity is incomprehensible, and#footnote[Acts 7:48,44; Acts 17:27; Jeremiah 23:23–24] every where present, it followeth necessarily that the same is without the bounds of his humane Nature which he took unto him, and yet is nevertheless in it,#footnote[Colossians 2:9; Matthew 28:6] and abideth personally united to it.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 48]: What Fruit doth the Ascension of Christ into Heaven bring unto us?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: First that#footnote[1 John 2:1–2; Romans 8:34] he maketh Intercession to his Father in Heaven for us; next that we have our Flesh in Heaven, that we may be confirmed thereby, as by a sure Pledge, that it shall come to passe that he who is our Head#footnote[John 14:2; John 20:17; Ephesians 2:6] will lift us up, his Members, unto him: thirdly, that#footnote[John 14:16; John 16:7; 2 Corinthians 5:5;] he sendeth us his Spirit instead of a Pledge between him and us, by whose forcible working we seek after not earthly but heavenly things, where he himself#footnote[Colossians 3:1; Philippians 3:20,&c] is sitting at the Right-Hand of God.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 49]: Why is it further said, he sitteth at the Right-Hand of God?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Because Christ therefore is ascended into Heaven, to#footnote[Ephesians 1:20; Ephesians 5:23; Colossians 1:18] shew there that he is the Head of his Church, by whom the Father#footnote[Matthew 28:18; John 5:22] governeth all things.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 50]: What profit is this Glory of our Head Christ unto us?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: First, that through his Holy Spirit#footnote[Ephesians 4:16] he poureth upon us his Members heavenly Graces, then that he shieldeth and#footnote[Psalm 2:9; Psalm 110:2; John 10:28; Ephesians 4:8] defendeth us by his Power against all our Enemies.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 51]: What Comfort hast thou by the coming of Christ again to judge the quick and the dead?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That in all my Miseries and Persecutions, I look with my#footnote[Luke 21:28; Romans 8:23; Philippians 3:20; Titus 2:13] Head lifted up, for the very same who before yielded himself unto the Judgment of God for#footnote[2 Thessalonians 1:6–7; 1 Thessalonians 4:16; Matthew 25:41] me, and took away all Malediction from me, to come Judge from Heaven to throw all his and my Enemies into everlasting Pains; but to#footnote[Matthew 25:34] translate me with all his chosen unto himself, into Celestiall Joys, and everlasting Glory.]
